       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and no recognized protocol uses sertraline at 1000 mg daily. That's five times the 200 mg/day maximum. Monitoring doesn't make that dose safe, because the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. A mistaken entry could reach the patient before anyone catches it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n\n- **Pharmacy:** Ask the reviewing pharmacist to enter or co-sign the order directly. They can also verify it through the hospital's own override process.\n- **Documentation:** If a protocol exists, send me its name or reference. I'd still want a prescriber-level override in the system rather than an entry from me.\n- **A different dose:** If the intended dose was lower, such as 100 mg, tell me and I'll enter it immediately."
      }
